    "narrative": "The offensive outlook for Ghost Ride the WHIP remains constrained today, with **Brice Turang** serving as our primary focal point against Nick Pivetta. **Turang** draws a marginal score of 47.07, anchored by his consistent recent production and the high-leverage utility of his sprint speed in a 5x5 format where steals are at a premium. While the 3.17 xERA of the opposing starter limits his ceiling, the platoon advantage (R vs R) and a favorable projected spot in the cleanup hole provide enough cushion to justify his presence in the starting lineup. We are prioritizing his ability to manufacture runs over pure slugging potential, keeping a close eye on his final placement in the order.\n\nOur most difficult decision involved **Dalton Rushing**, who ultimately landed on the bench with a score of 33.58. While the optimizer looked favorably upon his base projection, the matchup against Chris Sale (2.79 xERA) proved too daunting. The combination of a lefty-lefty disadvantage and an assumed bottom-of-the-order placement severely diluted his efficiency score, making him a risk we aren't willing to take with limited games remaining. With **Corbin Carroll**, **Jose Caballero**, and **Josh Naylor** all sitting during a team off-day, our bench lacks the depth to provide meaningful pivots. We are effectively playing a \"wait-and-see\" game, holding the rest of our roster\u2014including **James Wood**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Trevor Story**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Moises Ballesteros**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Griffin Conine**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Cole Young**\u2014in reserve until tomorrow\u2019s slate clears.",
